R"VG(
# industrial4.vg (H-04's second pass): more of the newspaper's columns (the works, an oddity, the town's health, the feast, the late
# years' small items) and its advertisements: things for sale and wanted, remedies, lessons and rooms, the town's shops, each in the
# people's own goods and coin.

ind.works
  The {craft} works at {$home} {ind.wk.news}.
  {ind.wk.lead} the {craft} trade {ind.wk.trade}.
  (has:$home.ptrade) {$home}, which lives by {$home.ptrade}, {ind.wk.town}.
ind.wk.news
  are taking on hands, and the queue at the gate began before light
  have gone on short time until the orders come back
  have a new boiler, and the neighbours have the noise of it
  will close for a week at {festival}, without pay
  have been sold to a company from {city}, which says nothing will change
ind.wk.lead
  This year in {$home}
  The guild reports that
  It is said in the yards that
ind.wk.trade
  has never been busier, nor its wages lower
  is losing its young people to the city
  will take no more apprentices until the price of {crop} comes down
  has found a buyer over the sea for everything it can make
ind.wk.town
  has had a better year than most
  is asking where the next one is to come from
  sends its thanks to the buyers of {city2}
  will hold its fair on the old day, whatever the council says
  (has:$home.landmark) has asked the council to mend {$home.landmark} before it falls on someone

ind.oddity
  {ind.odd.lead} {ind.odd.what}
  (has:$home.landmark) A {beast} has been living on {$home.landmark} since {season.now} began, and nobody can reach it.
  (has:$home.quarter) The people of {$home.quarter} have been woken every night this week by {ind.odd.noise}.
ind.odd.lead
  A curiosity from {$home}:
  Our readers will want to know that
  It is reported, and we pass it on, that
ind.odd.what
  a {beast} at the mill has learned to open the gate, and does.
  a {vessel.one.n} of {crop} left on a step at {$home} in {season.any} was found full of nests.
  a child of {$home} has counted the steps of {holyplace} and made them one more than the builders did.
  the {tree.n} by the north road flowered twice this year.
  a man has walked from the coast to {$home} backwards, for a bet, and won it.
  the bells of {holyplace} rang by themselves at midnight, and the ringers swear they were asleep.
ind.odd.noise
  a {beast} that will not stop
  {instrument} of someone practising
  the new engine at the works
  the {bird}, who have found the gutters

ind.health
  The doctors of {$home} {ind.hl.what}.
  A notice from the health board: {ind.hl.notice}.
ind.hl.what
  ask that water from the {watersrc.n} be boiled until further notice
  report fewer fevers than last {season.now}, and thank the new drains
  warn against the {food} sold from the carts at the station
  have vaccinated {nbig} children, and been bitten by {n}
ind.hl.notice
  the {pest} in the granaries are to be poisoned on the rest day; keep the {herd} in
  the public baths at {town.open} are open to women in the mornings
  nobody is to throw anything into the {watersrc.n} that they would not drink

ind.festival
  {festival} is near: {ind.fest.what}.
  The {festival} committee {ind.fest.cm}.
ind.fest.what
  the procession will take the [usual|old|long] route, and the band has been asked to [practise|keep together|start on time]
  {feast.custom} will be at {town.open} as always
  the stalls are let, and the {drink} brewed
  the children are rehearsing the songs, and the neighbours hearing them
ind.fest.cm
  reports that the fireworks have arrived and are being kept somewhere safe, away from the {fuel}
  asks for volunteers to carry the lamps in the procession
  has fixed the stall fees at {n} {smallcoin}, which the stallholders will discuss with it
  regrets that the {ind.sport} cannot be held this year

ind.late
  Another family has given up its house in the old town; the council is asked what it intends.
  The water rate goes up again next month, and the water has not improved.
  {n} houses in {streets.of} have stood empty since {season.now}, and the council will let them for nothing to anyone who will stay.
  The school will close one of its rooms; there are not the children to fill it.
  The {festival} fair will be held this year on one day only.
  (inv.railway=1) The night train has been cancelled for want of passengers.

# ---- the advertisements ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ind.ads
  {ind.ad}
  {ind.ad} {ind.ad}

ind.ad
  (once) For sale: {ind.sale}. {=.ad:sale}{ind.apply}
  (once) Wanted: {ind.wanted}. {=.ad:want}{ind.apply}
  (once) {ind.remedy.name}: {ind.remedy}.
  (once) Lessons on {instrument}, by a teacher lately of {ind.away}; {n} {smallcoin} the {ind.lesson.per}, {ind.lesson.extra}.
  (once) To let: {ind.let}. {=.ad:let}{ind.apply}
  (once) {ind.shop}
  (once) {craft} done cheaply and well. {=.ad:trade}{ind.apply}
  (once age>=modern) {ind.modern.ad}

ind.sale (share=0.6)
  {n} {herd} in good condition, the owner going over the sea
  a good cart, its wheels new, its owner old, with {n} {herd} to pull it
  a {colour.any} {garment.n}, worn once, at a funeral
  the tools of the {craft} trade, nearly new, the owner having taken up another
  {vessel} of every size, at the {craft} yard
  a stall at {town.open}, with the custom and the awning, in the {craft} row
  the right of the {watersrc.n} on the east side, with a bucket
  a {beast}, quiet, good with children, eats anything
  {n} {measure.load} of {crop}, dry, from last year
  a {ind.instr}, played by one careful owner
ind.wanted (share=0.6)
  a teacher for the school at {$home}, who must be able to read, and to teach {craft} besides
  hands for the {craft} works, no questions asked about the last place
  a girl for the dairy, early hours, {n} {smallcoin} a week and her {food}
  a clerk who can add, and will, at {n} {coin} a quarter
  a night watchman, sober, who is not afraid of {ind.wild}
  a strong boy for the {herd}, who can count them
  a cook for a house of {n}, plain food, {food} on the rest day
  a {ind.ct.trade}'s apprentice, the son of a {ind.ct.trade} preferred
# a paper's own way of saying where to apply (its house style: each paper keeps its few)
ind.apply (formula people=5)
  (.ad=want) Apply at the gate {time.of}.
  Enquire at the office of this paper.
  Apply to the clerk at {town.open}.
  (.ad=want) Write, giving your age and your references.
  (.ad=want) Apply in person, sober, to the foreman.
  Enquire at the inn by the market, and ask for the owner.
  Apply at the {ind.paper.name} office, by letter only.
  Ask at {holyplace}, after the service.
  Write to the box number below.
  (.ad=want) Apply before {festival}; no one taken after.
  (.ad=sale) Seen by appointment; no offers refused.
  (.ad=let) Rent by the season, paid in advance.
  (.ad=trade) Orders taken at the yard, {time.of}.
ind.let (share=0.6)
  rooms over the bakery, warm in winter, smelling of {food}
  a house by the {watersrc.n}, with a garden of {veg}
  a room for a single person of quiet habits and no {beast}
  a shop in the market row, the {craft} trade preferred
  a loft over the {craft} works, noisy by day, quiet by night
  {house.one} at the edge of the town, with a yard for {herd}
ind.remedy.name
  The {city} cordial
  Mother's balsam
  The old {$home} remedy
  The doctor's own drops
ind.remedy
  for coughs, colds, the [chest|back|liver] and the low spirits, {n} {smallcoin} the bottle
  cures the fever, the ague and the bad dreams; {n} {smallcoin}, from every chemist
  made of {crop2} and honey and something the makers will not say, which works
  taken by three generations of the {people}, and they are still here
ind.shop (share=0.6)
  The {$home} brewery: {drink}, [as your father drank it|brewed at the river|by the cup and by the cask].
  (coast=1) {fish}, fresh at the quay every morning, and cheaper after noon.
  The {$home} bakery has {food} on the rest day, for those who order before the bell.
  Boots made and mended at the sign of the {colour.any} {beast}.
  The {craft} shop by the bridge sells to the trade and to everyone else.
  {fruit} and {veg} from the hill farms, at the stall by {holyplace}, every market day.
  Lessons in {craft} for young women, by the widow of a master, at {n} {smallcoin} the {ind.lesson.per}.
ind.modern.ad
  Refrigerators on easy terms: keep your {food} as fresh as the day you bought it.
  The new motorcars are at the showroom by the station; drive one home to {ind.drive}.
  Learn to type in {n} weeks; the offices of {city} are waiting, and so are their {coin}.
  A wireless set in every house: {n} {coin} down and the rest when you can.
  (inv.telephone=1) Have a telephone put in, and never walk to {holyplace} to ask the time again.
ind.wild
  wolves
  the dark
  {game}
ind.instr
  drum
  fiddle
  set of pipes
  horn
ind.drive
  your door
  the country
  the coast
ind.lesson.per
  hour
  week
  season
ind.lesson.extra
  pupils of any age
  the neighbours permitting
  no talent required
  beginners in the mornings
)VG"
